  "raw_text": "Step 1: Let's denote the points as \\( A = (0, -1, -1) \\), \\( B = (-4, 4, 4) \\), and \\( C = (4, 5, 1) \\).\n\nStep 2: To find the equation of the plane, we need to determine a normal vector to the plane. We can do this by finding two vectors lying on the plane and then taking their cross product.\n\nStep 3: Calculate vector \\( \\overrightarrow{AB} \\):\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{AB} = B - A = (-4 - 0, 4 - (-1), 4 - (-1)) = (-4, 5, 5)\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Calculate vector \\( \\overrightarrow{AC} \\):\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{AC} = C - A = (4 - 0, 5 - (-1), 1 - (-1)) = (4, 6, 2)\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Compute the cross product \\( \\overrightarrow{AB} \\times \\overrightarrow{AC} \\):\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{AB} \\times \\overrightarrow{AC} = \\begin{vmatrix}\n\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\\n-4 & 5 & 5 \\\\\n4 & 6 & 2\n\\end{vmatrix}\n= \\mathbf{i}(5 \\cdot 2 - 5 \\cdot 6) - \\mathbf{j}(-4 \\cdot 2 - 5 \\cdot 4) + \\mathbf{k}(-4 \\cdot 6 - 5 \\cdot 4)\n= \\mathbf{i}(10 - 30) - \\mathbf{j}(-8 - 20) + \\mathbf{k}(-24 - 20)\n= -20\\mathbf{i} + 28\\mathbf{j} - 44\\mathbf{k}\n\\]\nSo, the normal vector is \\( \\langle -20, 28, -44 \\rangle \\).\n\nStep 6: Use the normal vector and one of the points to form the plane equation. Using point \\( A = (0, -1, -1) \\):\n\\[\n-20(x - 0) + 28(y + 1) - 44(z + 1) = 0\n\\]\nSimplify:\n\\[\n-20x + 28y + 28 - 44z - 44 = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n-20x + 28y - 44z - 16 = 0\n\\]\n\nStep 7: To ensure \\( A > 0 \\) and the greatest common divisor of the coefficients is 1, divide the entire equation by -4:\n\\[\n5x - 7y + 11z + 4 = 0\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{5x - 7y + 11z + 4 = 0}<|im_end|>",
